.TH DQL-EXPLAIN 1 "2026-07-05" "dql 0.1.0" "DelightQL Manual"
.SH NAME
dql-explain \- explain a DelightQL identifier (error, danger gate, or config)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dql explain
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.I IDENTIFIER
.SH DESCRIPTION
Looks the identifier up in the built-in registry and prints its badge
form, canonical URL, and prose explanation. Error records on stderr
carry these identifiers in brackets; this command is how you ask what
one means.
.PP
Accepted identifier forms:
.IP \(bu 3
badge form:
.B delightql\-error://semantic/cast
(kinds:
.BR error ", " danger ", " config );
.IP \(bu 3
canonical URL:
.BR https://delightql.org/uri/error/semantic/cast ;
.IP \(bu 3
bare hierarchy:
.B semantic/cast
(searched across all kinds).
.PP
Family nodes list their registered members.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 if the identifier resolved; 1 if it is not a DelightQL identifier
(the error lists the accepted forms).
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
$ dql query --db app.db 'nope(*)'
[delightql-error://semantic/resolution/table] Table not found: nope
$ dql explain semantic/resolution/table
delightql-error://semantic/resolution/table
  -> https://delightql.org/uri/error/semantic/resolution/table

A named table (or relation) was not found.
\&...
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dql (1),
.BR dql-query (1)
